wool|fibre|NOUN|Sheep's fibre|Soft hair from sheep, used to make yarn and cloth.|len; lông cừu|The blanket is woven from wool.|Chăn được dệt từ len.|Uncountable material; source core sheep fibre.|0
wind|air|NOUN|Moving air|Air moving outdoors across the Earth's surface.|gió|The wind shook the branches.|Gió làm rung cành cây.|Often uncountable; winds for types.|0
wind|curve|VERB|Follow a curving course|To follow a route with repeated bends.|uốn lượn|The path winds between the trees.|Lối đi uốn lượn giữa các cây.|Wind, wound, wound; verb pronunciation differs from air noun.|1
wind|wrap|VERB|Wrap around|To wrap something around another object by turning it.|quấn; cuốn|She wound the thread around the spool.|Cô ấy quấn chỉ quanh ống chỉ.|Wind something around; past wound.|2
wind|mechanism|VERB|Tighten a mechanism|To turn a mechanism so it stores energy to operate.|lên dây cót|He wound the old clock before bed.|Anh ấy lên dây cót đồng hồ cũ trước khi ngủ.|Wind a clock; past wound.|3
worried|anxious|ADJECTIVE|Feeling concern|Feeling anxious about a possible problem.|lo lắng|She looked worried about the exam.|Cô ấy có vẻ lo về kỳ thi.|Worried about.|0
wrist|joint|NOUN|Joint beside the hand|The joint connecting the hand to the forearm.|cổ tay|The bracelet slipped over her wrist.|Chiếc vòng trượt qua cổ tay cô ấy.|Countable; history protected.|0
worship|noun|NOUN|Religious honour|Religious acts expressing reverence for a deity or sacred figure.|sự thờ phụng|The building is used for worship.|Tòa nhà được dùng cho việc thờ phụng.|Uncountable activity.|0
worship|verb|VERB|Honour religiously|To show religious reverence through belief or practice.|thờ phụng|The community worships in the small temple.|Cộng đồng thờ phụng tại ngôi đền nhỏ.|Transitive or intransitive.|1
